          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "**Yes.** The records identify a component-issue event for September manufacturing order **MO-25-09-1070** that was created **145 minutes after** the September cost period entered Pending Close.\n\n### Event identified\n\n| Item | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| Work order | **WO-2025-09-004** — **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine — Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25** (`PER-COST-2025-09`) |\n| Cost event | `CE-250904-0004` |\n| Source transaction | **TXN-ISSUE-250930-1070** |\n| Event type | `INPUT` — component issue |\n| Amount | **US$318,250.75** (**31,825,075 cents**) |\n| Event-created time | **2025-09-30T20:25:00** |\n| Period entered Pending Close | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** |\n| Delay | **2 hours 25 minutes = 145 minutes** |\n| Recorded accounting status | **POSTED** |\n\nThe calculation is **8,700 seconds ÷ 60 = 145 minutes**. Timestamps are reproduced exactly as recorded; the source does not specify a time zone.\n\n### Policy-consistency conclusion\n\n**The recorded `POSTED` status is not consistent with Oracle’s documented Pending Close treatment on the supplied records.**\n\nOracle states that newly created transactions falling in the current or an earlier period **will not be staged or processed after Pending Close until the period is closed or reopened**. Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions; this `INPUT` component issue is not one of them.\n\n**Policy source:** *Oracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B*, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” printed page **225**, PDF page **233**.\n\n### Evidence and delivery note\n\nThe work-order and period facts came from the task records; the event came from the cached supporting-record package explicitly associated with this job. The primary supporting-record endpoint was not staged. The report was submitted, but automated evidence review remains **`needs_evidence`**, not validated.\n\nThe review was read-only; **no database records were changed**. The audit result and provenance are saved at:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_bd009bcc1287/audit-report.json`",
